/*
  VisuallyHidden.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0003 · VisuallyHidden (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/a11y/VisuallyHidden.tsx) is anonymous — it renders content invisible to sighted
  users but exposed to assistive technology and extracts no `t()` keys — so every key here is
  native chrome: the inspector title, the three render-mode names + summaries, the ARIA token
  captions, the element-kind row, the recent-history heading, the VoiceOver wording, and the
  P4 leaf freshness / loading / empty / error copy, so the Swift sources hold no English
  literals. These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at
  integration time; they are kept in a per-surface table ("VisuallyHidden") so each parallel
  surface prompt owns its own strings without editing the shared catalog.
*/

/* --- Surface header --- */
"vh.title" = "Visually hidden";
"vh.subtitle" = "Content exposed to assistive technology without a visual footprint";

/* --- Hidden mode (the bare sr-only default) --- */
"vh.hidden.title" = "Hidden";
